  "verbalization": "Oxitriptan is implicated in the relationship with C8166 through a series of molecular interactions. The drug is directly linked to the 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 1, which is targeted by Licoricesaponin G2 and 7,10-Epoxy-Ar-Bisabol-11-Ol. These compounds, in turn, target C8166, suggesting a potential pathway where Oxitriptan may modulate the activity of the 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 1 through interaction with these secondary ligands. The evidence suggests a mechanistic link between Oxitriptan and C8166, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated. The scores from the paths indicate a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct involvement of Oxitriptan in the regulation of C8166.",
